IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coq-common`
IMPORT `coq-body`

-- Coroners Act 2003 (Queensland) -- worked cases for coq-body.l4 (ss 19-26, 95).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (act-2003-013, in force from 2026-10-29), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario
-- life raised this Act; the facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Every "considers" and "is satisfied" of
-- a coroner is given as a fact.
--
-- A breached DEONTIC cannot be compared with EQUALS on the stable l4, so the s 24(6) rule is asserted through the
-- questions that use CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED, and one breach is #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`dmy` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

§ `s 19(5), (6) -- my concern about an internal autopsy`

-- Argument order: s 19 excluded, examination, family member or sufficient interest, raised a concern, still ordered.
#ASSERT `My concern about an internal autopsy question` TRUE `an external and full internal examination` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 19 does not apply: the coroner has stopped investigating, or is investigating a suspected death (s 19(1))`
#ASSERT `My concern about an internal autopsy question` FALSE `an external examination only` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 19(5) does not apply: it applies only before an internal examination is ordered`
#ASSERT `My concern about an internal autopsy question` FALSE `an examination of cremated remains` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 19(5) does not apply: it applies only before an internal examination is ordered`
#ASSERT `My concern about an internal autopsy question` FALSE `an external and partial internal examination` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 19(5)(b) does not apply: it covers concerns raised by a family member or another person with a sufficient interest`
#ASSERT `My concern about an internal autopsy question` FALSE `an external and full internal examination` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner must, whenever practicable, consider the family's possible distress (s 19(5)(a)); you have raised no concern for s 19(5)(b)`
-- A family who object on religious grounds to a full internal examination.
#ASSERT `My concern about an internal autopsy question` FALSE `an external and partial internal examination` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner must, whenever practicable, consider your concern before ordering the internal examination (s 19(5)(b))`
#ASSERT `My concern about an internal autopsy question` FALSE `an external and full internal examination` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the coroner considered your concern and still ordered the internal examination: you must be given a copy of the order (s 19(6))`

§ `s 20(3)-(5) -- notice before an exhumation`

-- Argument order: in charge of the place, sufficient interest, could not be contacted, notice not in the public interest.
#ASSERT `Must I be told before an exhumation question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 20(3) requires notice only to the person in charge of the place and to persons the State Coroner considers have a sufficient interest in the autopsy`
#ASSERT `Must I be told before an exhumation question` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the State Coroner must give you at least 2 days notice of the intended order (s 20(3)); if you raise a concern and, after discussing it with you, the State Coroner still considers the order in the public interest, you must be given a copy of the order (s 20(5))`
#ASSERT `Must I be told before an exhumation question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the State Coroner must give you at least 2 days notice of the intended order (s 20(3)); if you raise a concern and, after discussing it with you, the State Coroner still considers the order in the public interest, you must be given a copy of the order (s 20(5))`
#ASSERT `Must I be told before an exhumation question` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 20(3) does not apply, as the State Coroner could not contact you after taking all reasonable steps (s 20(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must I be told before an exhumation question` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 20(3) does not apply, as the State Coroner considers notifying you is not in the public interest (s 20(4)(b))`
-- Notice on 10 January 2027: the order may be made from 12 January (fork F6); across a year end.
#ASSERT `Earliest day for the exhumation order question` (`dmy` 10 1 2027) EQUALS `dmy` 12 1 2027
#ASSERT `Earliest day for the exhumation order question` (`dmy` 30 12 2026) EQUALS `dmy` 1 1 2027

§ `s 21(3)-(5) -- observing the autopsy`

#ASSERT `Can I observe the autopsy question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the coroner has allowed you, or your representative, to observe; you must be given notice of the time and place before the autopsy (s 21(3), (5))`
#ASSERT `Can I observe the autopsy question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `possibly: the coroner may allow you, or your representative, to observe (s 21(3)), after consulting a family member and the doctor whenever practicable (s 21(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I observe the autopsy question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 21(3) does not let the coroner allow it unless the coroner considers you have a sufficient interest, your attendance would not compromise any investigation, and it is otherwise appropriate`
-- A relative who is a suspect in a homicide investigation: attendance would compromise it.
#ASSERT `Can I observe the autopsy question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 21(3) does not let the coroner allow it unless the coroner considers you have a sufficient interest, your attendance would not compromise any investigation, and it is otherwise appropriate`
#ASSERT `Can I observe the autopsy question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 21(3) does not let the coroner allow it unless the coroner considers you have a sufficient interest, your attendance would not compromise any investigation, and it is otherwise appropriate`

§ `s 23A -- asking for an autopsy test`

-- A paramedic pricked by a needle while treating the person who died asks for a blood-borne virus test.
#ASSERT `Can I get an autopsy test question` `a test for an infectious, notifiable, emergency notifiable or controlled notifiable condition` TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may apply in writing and the coroner may order the test (s 23A(1), (2)); you may then have access to the result (s 52(1)(c)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can I get an autopsy test question` `a test for an infectious, notifiable, emergency notifiable or controlled notifiable condition` FALSE EQUALS `no: the coroner may grant the application only if satisfied you have a sufficient interest in the test result (s 23A(2))`
-- A family wanting a genetic test for an inherited heart condition: not a s 23A test.
#ASSERT `Can I get an autopsy test question` `another test` TRUE EQUALS `not under s 23A, which covers only tests for infectious and notifiable conditions; the coroner may still order a test on the coroner's own initiative (s 23(2))`

§ `ss 24(4), (5), 26 -- the release of the body`

-- Argument order: autopsy done, no longer needed, identity known, burial necessary, prescribed tissue removed, family
-- told (or not practicable), coroner satisfied keeping is necessary.
#ASSERT `Will the body be released question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: this question covers the release after an autopsy (s 26(2)(f)); the other paths of s 26(2) are not encoded`
#ASSERT `Will the body be released question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: the coroner keeps control of the body until deciding it is no longer needed for the investigation (s 26(2)(f))`
#ASSERT `Will the body be released question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the coroner must not order the release for burial while it is not known whose body it is, unless the coroner believes burial is necessary (s 26(4))`
#ASSERT `Will the body be released question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the coroner must order the release of the body for burial as soon as reasonably practicable after the autopsy (s 26(2)(f), (3))`
#ASSERT `Will the body be released question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the coroner must order the release of the body for burial as soon as reasonably practicable after the autopsy (s 26(2)(f), (3))`
-- The heart kept for specialist examination, the family told: released without it.
#ASSERT `Will the body be released question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, without the organs or body parts kept: a family member has been told (if practicable) and the coroner is satisfied keeping them is necessary (s 24(4)); the coroner must order the release as soon as reasonably practicable (s 26(3)) and review the kept tissue at most every 6 months (s 24(6))`
-- The family not told although it was practicable: the organ goes back with the body.
#ASSERT `Will the body be released question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, with the organs or body parts kept returned to it: the coroner is not satisfied of s 24(4)(a) and (b), so must order the doctor to return them to the body before it is released (s 24(5)); and must order the release as soon as reasonably practicable (s 26(3))`
#ASSERT `Will the body be released question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, with the organs or body parts kept returned to it: the coroner is not satisfied of s 24(4)(a) and (b), so must order the doctor to return them to the body before it is released (s 24(5)); and must order the release as soon as reasonably practicable (s 26(3))`

§ `s 24(6) -- the 6-monthly review of kept tissue`

-- Order of 15 January 2027: the decision is due by 15 July 2027.
#ASSERT `Last day for the tissue decision question` (`dmy` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `dmy` 15 7 2027
-- Order of 31 August 2026: 6 months on is 28 February 2027 (no 31 February); from 31 August 2027, 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `Last day for the tissue decision question` (`dmy` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `dmy` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `Last day for the tissue decision question` (`dmy` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `dmy` 29 2 2028
-- Decided on the last day; a day late; not yet decided on the last day; not decided the day after.
#ASSERT `Tissue decision in time question` (`dmy` 15 1 2027) TRUE (`dmy` 15 7 2027) (`dmy` 1 8 2027) EQUALS `yes: the coroner did it within the period the Act allows`
#ASSERT `Tissue decision in time question` (`dmy` 15 1 2027) TRUE (`dmy` 16 7 2027) (`dmy` 1 8 2027) EQUALS `no: the coroner did it, but after the period the Act allows had ended`
#ASSERT `Tissue decision in time question` (`dmy` 15 1 2027) FALSE (`dmy` 1 1 2027) (`dmy` 15 7 2027) EQUALS `not yet due: the coroner has not done it, but the period has not ended`
#ASSERT `Tissue decision in time question` (`dmy` 15 1 2027) FALSE (`dmy` 1 1 2027) (`dmy` 16 7 2027) EQUALS `overdue: the period the Act allows has ended and the coroner has not done it`
#ASSERT `Tissue decision in time question` (`dmy` 31 8 2026) TRUE (`dmy` 28 2 2027) (`dmy` 1 8 2027) EQUALS `yes: the coroner did it within the period the Act allows`
#ASSERT `Tissue decision in time question` (`dmy` 31 8 2026) TRUE (`dmy` 1 3 2027) (`dmy` 1 8 2027) EQUALS `no: the coroner did it, but after the period the Act allows had ended`
-- The rule itself, over 181 days (15 January to 15 July 2027): kept on day 181, broken when day 182 passes without it.
#ASSERT `decide whether the prescribed tissue still needs to be kept` `done at` 181 `is in time under` (`s 24(6) -- decide on the kept tissue within the interval` 181)
#ASSERT NOT (`decide whether the prescribed tissue still needs to be kept` `done at` 182 `is in time under` (`s 24(6) -- decide on the kept tissue within the interval` 181))
#TRACE `s 24(6) -- decide on the kept tissue within the interval` 181 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 182)
-- expect: BREACH BY `the coroner` BECAUSE "s 24(6): ..."

§ `s 24(7)-(9) -- the kept tissue`

-- Argument order: specimen tissue, disposal ordered, I am the family member, I told the coroner my wish.
#ASSERT `What happens to the kept tissue question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `it must be kept indefinitely: it has been made into specimen tissue (s 24(7))`
#ASSERT `What happens to the kept tissue question` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `it must be kept: it must not be disposed of except under a coroner's order (s 24(8))`
-- A family who want to bury the heart with the body's ashes.
#ASSERT `What happens to the kept tissue question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `it must be released to you, or your representative, for the test, use or burial you told the coroner of (s 24(9)(a))`
#ASSERT `What happens to the kept tissue question` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it must be buried, as no family member has told the coroner of a wish to test, use or bury it (s 24(9)(b))`
-- A friend who is not the family member.
#ASSERT `What happens to the kept tissue question` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `it must be buried, as no family member has told the coroner of a wish to test, use or bury it (s 24(9)(b))`

§ `s 95 -- burial, cremation, or taking the body out of Queensland`

-- Argument order: who is investigating, certificate issued, coroner consented, release ordered, outside release
-- certificate.
#ASSERT `May we bury the body question` `a Queensland coroner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you are authorised, as a cause of death certificate has been issued with the coroner's consent (s 95(2)(a)(i))`
-- A certificate issued without the investigating coroner's consent does not authorise the funeral.
#ASSERT `May we bury the body question` `a Queensland coroner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you must not prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland until authorised under s 95(2); maximum penalty 120 penalty units (s 95(1))`
#ASSERT `May we bury the body question` `a Queensland coroner` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you are authorised, as the coroner has ordered the release of the body (s 95(2)(a)(ii))`
#ASSERT `May we bury the body question` `a Queensland coroner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you must not prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland until authorised under s 95(2); maximum penalty 120 penalty units (s 95(1))`
#ASSERT `May we bury the body question` `a coroner outside Queensland` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you are authorised, as a non-Queensland coroner's release certificate has been issued (s 95(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `May we bury the body question` `a coroner outside Queensland` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you must not prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland until authorised under s 95(2); maximum penalty 120 penalty units (s 95(1))`
#ASSERT `May we bury the body question` `no coroner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you are authorised, as a cause of death certificate has been issued (s 95(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `May we bury the body question` `no coroner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you must not prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland until authorised under s 95(2); maximum penalty 120 penalty units (s 95(1))`
